        "title": "Grid-Scale Storage Economics: LCOS, Learning Curves, and Revenue Stacking",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "Energy storage economics are often summarized by Levelized Cost of Storage (LCOS),\nbut bankable projects are decided by revenue timing, market rules, degradation,\nfinancing, and contractability. Li-ion learning curves have been extraordinary;\ngrid storage economics still require matching the asset to a revenue stack it can\nactually deliver."
